WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.080
Communications and user activity artifacts are often central to Android investigations.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:19.620
SMS and MMS records, call logs, contacts, messaging applications, email applications, browser records, notifications, app usage indicators, keyboard artifacts, and autofill-related traces can all provide context.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:25.120
The challenge is not merely finding artifacts; it is interpreting what they mean and what they do not mean.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:37.260
Traditional phone artifacts such as SMS, MMS, call logs, and contacts may show communication events, participants, timestamps, and sometimes message content or metadata.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.560
Even here, caution is needed.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:44.980
A call log may show an attempted, missed, or completed call depending on the fields available.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:51.120
A contact record may be created by user action, account sync, import, or an application feature.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:59.260
Messaging and email applications add complexity because many are cloud-backed, encrypted, multi-device, or account-centered.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:07.480
Local app data may represent cached messages, notifications, drafts, attachments, account metadata, or sync state.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.020
It may not contain the complete conversation.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.760
It may also include material received on the account but not necessarily viewed on the specific device.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:19.820
Browser and notification artifacts can be useful but easy to overstate.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:31.560
Browser history, downloads, cookies, cached pages, search suggestions, and tabs may reflect user activity, background loading, redirects, embedded content, or synchronized browsing state.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:39.220
Notifications may reveal that an event reached the device, but not always whether the user saw, opened, dismissed, or acted on it.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:44.800
A disciplined analyst separates local device artifacts from cloud-synced or account-based activity.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:51.660
They avoid claiming that a specific person performed a specific action unless the evidence supports that level of attribution.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:02:02.680
Communications artifacts are strongest when they are correlated with account logs, device unlock context, timestamps, app records, network evidence, and other independent sources.
